---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="How FCMOBILETOOLS uses cookies, browser storage, analytics and advertising technologies.">
  <article class="wrap legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">LEGAL / COOKIES</p>
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">Last updated: October 9, 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2>What cookies are</h2>
      <p>Cookies are small files that a website or service can save in your browser. Similar technologies can remember preferences, keep a session active, measure site use or support advertising. Some tools may also save settings or progress in your browser.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Necessary site functions</h2>
      <p>Cookies or browser storage may be used to remember your privacy choices, support sign-in, keep features working and help protect the site. Blocking or clearing them may reset saved preferences, remove local tool progress or sign you out.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>We use Google Analytics on pages where it is installed to understand visits and improve the site. Depending on your choices and settings, analytics services may use cookies or similar technologies to measure page views and general usage.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>The site may display ads provided by Google. Google and its advertising partners may use cookies, web beacons, IP addresses or similar identifiers to deliver ads, measure performance, limit repeated ads, prevent abuse or personalise ads according to your settings and applicable consent choices.</p>
      <p>Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from partner sites</a> and manage ad personalisation through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Managing your choices</h2>
      <p>Use the <strong>Privacy Choices</strong> link in the site footer where available to review the privacy options offered on the site. You can also block or clear cookies through your browser settings. Your choices may affect some features, and rejecting optional storage may not prevent every connection to an external service needed to load a page.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>External services and updates</h2>
      <p>Pages may include content or links from external services, such as videos, images or advertisements. Those providers may use their own technologies under their own policies. We may update this policy when our site features or service providers change.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
